
==============================================================================
18.1 Which way and how fast (multiple choice)
==============================================================================
p = 5 cos(2pi 1e8 t + 0.8 pi x): v = [-2.5e+08 -0.0e+00 -0.0e+00] m/s -> -x speed 2.5000e+08
q = u(0.004 z - t):              v = [  0.   0. 250.] m/s -> +z speed 250
r = exp(-(t + 0.0125 y)^2):      v = [ -0. -80.  -0.] m/s -> -y speed 80
  t = 0 s: edge of q at z = 0.000 m; peak of r at y = 0.000 m
  t = 1 s: edge of q at z = 250.000 m; peak of r at y = -80.000 m
  t = 2 s: edge of q at z = 500.000 m; peak of r at y = -160.000 m
  t = 0 ns: crest (phase 0) of p at x = 0.0000 m
  t = 1 ns: crest (phase 0) of p at x = -0.2500 m
  t = 2 ns: crest (phase 0) of p at x = -0.5000 m
  slownesses: q 0.004 s/m -> 1/0.004 = 250 m/s; r 0.0125 s/m -> 80 m/s
  p slower than c: non-magnetic eps_r = (c/v)^2 = 1.4380 (c = 3e8: 1.4400)
  options: (a) +2.5e8 x, +250 z, -80 y  (b) -2.5e8 x, -250 z, -80 y  (c) -2.5e8 x, +250 z, -80 y [correct]
           (d) -2.5e8 x, +0.004 z, -0.0125 y  (e) -2.5e8 x, +250 z, +80 y

==============================================================================
18.2 The partner field (free space)
==============================================================================
(a) E = 6 y cos(w(t - z/c)):  u = +z
  z x y = [-1.  0.  0.]  (-x)
    |H| = 6/eta0 = 15.927 mA/m (120pi: 15.915); |B| = 6/c = 20.014 nT
  E(y) x H(-x) = [ 0. -0.  1.]  (+z)
  [18.2a] Faraday rel.res 2.9e-10 | Ampere-Maxwell 2.9e-10 | div/curl 0.0e+00 | wave eq E 2.4e-09, H 3.5e-09  -> OK
(b) E = 3 x exp(-((t + y/c)/tau)^2):  u = -y
  (-y) x x = [0. 0. 1.]  (+z)
    |H| = 3/eta0 = 7.963 mA/m; |B| = 3/c = 10.007 nT
  E(x) x H(+z) = [ 0. -1.  0.]  (-y)
  [18.2b] Faraday rel.res 3.1e-10 | Ampere-Maxwell 2.8e-10 | div/curl 0.0e+00 | wave eq E 2.2e-07, H 7.2e-08  -> OK
(c) H = 0.05 z cos(w(t - x/c)) A/m:  u = +x;  E = eta0 H x u
  z x x = [0. 1. 0.]  (+y)
    |E| = eta0*0.05 = 18.837 V/m (120pi: 18.850); |B| = mu0*0.05 = 62.832 nT = E/c = 62.832 nT
  E(+y) x H(z) = [1. 0. 0.]  (+x)
    check also H = u x E/eta0: [0. 0. 1.] = z
  [18.2c] Faraday rel.res 3.4e-10 | Ampere-Maxwell 3.3e-10 | div/curl 0.0e+00 | wave eq E 2.9e-09, H 3.1e-09  -> OK

==============================================================================
18.3 Phase rate and snapshot period (SP18 Exam 2 #1(vii) style)
==============================================================================
omega = 6pi/10 ns = 1.8850e+09 rad/s (= 6pi x 1e8); beta = 2pi/0.4 = 15.7080 rad/m (= 5pi)
v = omega/beta = 1.2000e+08 m/s; temporal period 2pi/omega = 3.3333 ns; 0.4 m / period = 1.2000e+08
eps_r = (c/v)^2 = 6.2414 (c = 3e8: 6.2500); eta = mu0 v = 150.796 Ohm = 48.000 pi; eta0/sqrt(eps_r) = 150.796
H amplitude = 12/eta = 79.577 mA/m; B = 12/v = 100.000 nT = mu0 H = 100.000 nT
  u(+x) x E(y) = [0. 0. 1.]  (+z)
  E(y) x H(z) = [1. 0. 0.]  (+x)
  [18.3] Faraday rel.res 1.2e-10 | Ampere-Maxwell 6.6e-10 | div/curl 0.0e+00 | wave eq E 1.2e-08, H 8.6e-09  -> OK

==============================================================================
18.4 What the derivation needs (true or false)
==============================================================================
(a) travelling wave: lap E_x = -4.3151, -(w/v)^2 E_x = -4.3151  -> lap E != 0, so it cannot satisfy Laplace's equation (what remains without dD/dt)
(b) div(eps E) = rho check: eps*dEx/dx = 7.0000e-10 vs rho = 7.0000e-10
    lap E - mu eps d2E/dt2 = [2.82352e+01 1.00000e-04 0.00000e+00]; grad(rho)/eps = [28.2352  0.      0.    ]  -> extra term, statement FALSE
(c) div D = 0.000e+00 (zero); div E at x=0 = -2.00000 V/m^2 = -E0/a = -2.00000  -> FALSE
(d) E = z cos(w(t - z/v)): 1D wave-equation rel. residual 6.5e-10 (solves it), but div E = 0.0433 vs (w/v) sin(.) = 0.0433  -> violates Gauss (rho = 0): FALSE
    and curl E = [0. 0. 0.] -> Faraday gives no H partner

==============================================================================
18.5 Find the error: H pointing the wrong way
==============================================================================
E = z 12 cos(1.5pi e8 t + 2pi x): same signs -> travels -x; v = 7.5000e+07 m/s; eps_r = 15.978 (c=3e8: 16.000)
eta = mu0 v = 94.248 Ohm = 30.000 pi (eta0/4 = 94.183); |H| = 12/eta = 0.12732 A/m = 127.3 mA/m
  u(-x) x z = [0. 1. 0.]  (+y)
  z x u(-x) = [ 0. -1.  0.]  (-y)
  E(z) x H_correct = [-1.  0.  0.]  (-x)
  E(z) x H_student = [ 1.  0. -0.]  (+x)
  [18.5 correct H = +y] Faraday rel.res 7.0e-11 | Ampere-Maxwell 6.4e-10 | div/curl 0.0e+00 | wave eq E 2.5e-07, H 2.6e-07  -> OK
  [18.5 student's H = -y] Faraday rel.res 2.00 (2 = opposite sign) -> FAILS

==============================================================================
18.6 Which fields can be waves (mu eps = 1e-16 s^2/m^2, mu = mu0)
==============================================================================
v = 1/sqrt(mu eps) = 1.0000e+08 m/s; eps_r = 8.9876; eta = mu0 v = 125.6637 Ohm = 40.0000 pi
  E1 = 4 cos(2e8 t - 2z)                     max rel. residual of d2/dz2 - mu eps d2/dt2: 6.11e-08 -> SOLVES
  E2 = 4 cos(2e8 t) cos(2z)                  max rel. residual of d2/dz2 - mu eps d2/dt2: 2.41e-08 -> SOLVES
  E3 = 4 cos(2e8 t - 6z)                     max rel. residual of d2/dz2 - mu eps d2/dt2: 8.89e-01 -> fails
  E4 = 4 cos(2e8 t - 2z) cos(2e8 t + 2z)     max rel. residual of d2/dz2 - mu eps d2/dt2: 1.84e+00 -> fails
  omega^2 = (2e8)^2 = 4e+16 rad^2/s^2; beta^2 = 4; mu eps omega^2 = 4
  E3: d2/dz2 = -36 E, mu eps d2/dt2 = -4 E; own speed 2e8/6 = 3.3333e+07 m/s; needs mu eps = 9.0e-16 -> eps_r = 80.89
  E4 = 2cos(4z) + 2cos(4e8 t): at z = 0, t = pi/4e8 = 7.8540 ns: d2/dz2 = -32.0, mu eps d2/dt2 = 32.0
  E4 identity check: True
(b) H for E2: H_y = (E0/eta) sin(wt) sin(bz), E0/eta = 0.031831 A/m = 31.83 mA/m (= 1/(10 pi) = 0.031831)
  [18.6 standing pair (E2, H2)] Faraday rel.res 7.0e-10 | Ampere-Maxwell 6.9e-10 | div/curl 0.0e+00 | wave eq E 1.1e-06, H 2.0e-06  -> OK
  with the opposite sign of H: Faraday rel.res 2.00 (fails)
(c) E2 = 2cos(wt-bz) + 2cos(wt+bz): True ; H = (2/eta)[cos(wt-bz) - cos(wt+bz)] = H2: True
    each travelling part: E amplitude 2 V/m, H amplitude 2/eta = 15.92 mA/m
(d) E = 0 everywhere when w t = pi/2: t = 7.8540 ns; then H_y = 31.83 sin(2z) mA/m, largest at z = pi/4 = 0.7854 m (and every pi/2 = 1.5708 m)
    E2 nodes (E = 0 at all t): cos(2z) = 0 -> z = pi/4 + n pi/2; H2 nodes: sin(2z) = 0 -> z = n pi/2

==============================================================================
18.7 A cable and its filling (parallel strips W = 8 mm, d = 1 mm)
==============================================================================
v = 3 m / 18 ns = 1.66667e+08 m/s; eps_r = (c/v)^2 = 3.2355 (c = 3e8: 3.2400 = 1.8^2)
eta = mu0 v = 209.440 Ohm; eta0/1.8 = 209.295; 120pi/1.8 = 209.440
  eps_r = 3.2400: C' = eps W/d = 229.50 pF/m; L' = mu0 d/W = 157.08 nH/m (0.1571 uH/m); 1/sqrt(L'C') = 1.66551e+08 m/s; sqrt(L'/C') = 26.162 Ohm; eta d/W = 26.162 Ohm; L'C' = 3.6050e-17 = mu eps = 3.6050e-17
  eps_r = 3.2355: C' = eps W/d = 229.18 pF/m; L' = mu0 d/W = 157.08 nH/m (0.1571 uH/m); 1/sqrt(L'C') = 1.66667e+08 m/s; sqrt(L'/C') = 26.180 Ohm; eta d/W = 26.180 Ohm; L'C' = 3.6000e-17 = mu eps = 3.6000e-17
coax with the same sqrt(L'/C'): (eta/2pi) ln(b/a) = eta d/W -> ln(b/a) = 2pi d/W = 0.7854 (pi/4); b/a = 2.1933
  coax L' = 157.08 nH/m, C' = 229.50 pF/m (identical to the strips); delay over 3 m = 18.01 ns (with c=3e8 eps_r: 18.0 ns)
  sqrt(L'/C') coax = 26.162 Ohm

